* dsPIC33FJ128MC802 family -- Pin Definitions file for QSymGen3
* Source: Microchip DS70291G, "dsPIC33FJ32MC302/304, dsPIC33FJ64MCX02/X04,
* and dsPIC33FJ128MCX02/X04 Data Sheet"
* Package: 28-Pin SPDIP/SOIC (pin numbers below refer to this pinout)
* Covers dsPIC33FJ128MC802, dsPIC33FJ128MC202, dsPIC33FJ64MC802,
* dsPIC33FJ64MC202, dsPIC33FJ32MC302 -- all five share this exact
* pinout in both the 28-Pin SPDIP/SOIC and 28-Pin QFN-S diagrams.
*
* NOTE: AVDD, AVSS, and VCAP (flagged individually below) have no
* proper record type in the current .qpindef format. AVDD/AVSS are
* electrically distinct from VDD/VSS (separate analog supply/ground
* per the datasheet) but the format allows only one V and one G
* record; VCAP is a regulator filter-cap node, not a supply, ground,
* or signal pin at all. All three are provisionally typed I pending
* a decision on how QSymGen3 should represent them.
*
D 16-bit Digital Signal Controllers (up to 128 KB Flash and 16K SRAM) with Motor Control PWM and Advanced Analog
P dsPIC33FJ128MC802 dsPIC33FJ128MC202 dsPIC33FJ64MC802 dsPIC33FJ64MC202 dsPIC33FJ32MC302
*
V VDD
*
* FLAG: AVDD (pin 28) -- see AVDD/AVSS/VCAP note above. Provisionally I.
I AVDD
*
* FLAG: AVSS (pin 27) -- see AVDD/AVSS/VCAP note above. Provisionally I.
I AVSS
*
* FLAG: MCLR (pin 1) -- device Reset input ("Master Clear (Reset) input.
* This pin is an active-low Reset to the device."). Table lists it as
* type I/P, not a general-purpose GPIO. Classified I; flagged per
* procedure since RESET pins are explicitly called out as non-obvious.
I MCLR
*
B RA0 AN0/VREF+/CN2
B RA1 AN1/VREF-/CN3
B RA2 OSC1/CLKI/CN30
B RA3 OSC2/CLKO/CN29/PMA0
B RA4 SOSCO/T1CK/CN0/PMA1
B RB0 PGED1/AN2/C2IN-/RP0/CN4
B RB1 PGEC1/AN3/C2IN+/RP1/CN5
B RB2 AN4/C1IN-/RP2/CN6
B RB3 AN5/C1IN+/RP3/CN7
*
K SIMCLK
*
B RB4 SOSCI/RP4/CN1/PMBE
B RB5 PGED3/ASDA1/RP5/CN27/PMD7
B RB6 PGEC3/ASCL1/RP6/CN24/PMD6
B RB7 INT0/RP7/CN23/PMD5
B RB8 TCK/PWM2H1/SCL1/RP8/CN22/PMD4
B RB9 TDO/PWM2L1/SDA1/RP9/CN21/PMD3
B RB10 PGED2/TDI/PWM1H3/RP10/CN16/PMD2
B RB11 PGEC2/TMS/PWM1L3/RP11/CN15/PMD1
B RB12 PWM1H2/RP12/CN14/PMD0
B RB13 PWM1L2/RP13/CN13/PMRD
B RB14 PWM1H1/RTCC/RP14/CN12/PMWR
B RB15 PWM1L1/RP15/CN11/PMCS1
*
* FLAG: VCAP (pin 20) -- see AVDD/AVSS/VCAP note above. Provisionally I.
* Must NOT be tied to the VDD/VSS net -- it's a distinct decoupling
* node, not a duplicate power pin.
I VCAP
*
* Pin 19 (VSS) is a second physical VSS pin -- same net as the VSS
* record below (pin 8). No second record created (duplicate-pin rule).
G VSS
